---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Cookies on NZ Salary: What Is Set in Your Browser" description="Cookies and local storage on NZ Salary: none for the calculators, your choice if audience measurement is ever enabled, and how to change or withdraw it at any time." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Cookies', path: route('cookies', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Cookies</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <p>The calculators do not use cookies. They keep your inputs only in the page itself, and in the address bar when you use the share link.</p>
    <p>No analytics or advertising cookie is set today. If audience measurement is added, a notice will inform you before anything is loaded, your choice will be kept in your browser’s local storage under the key <code>consent-choice</code>, and a link at the bottom of every page will let you change it.</p>
    <p>Questions: see the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
